 "post_instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Listening", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}], "type": "learning_skills"}], "id": 12, "type": "TAB"}], "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}], "type": "lab_options"}], "stimuli": [{"_data": [], "type": "welcome", "template_override": 1, "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "contents": [{"value": {"coverimg": "enpe7n2le01ob05re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"time": "100", "text": "<strong>Pablo</strong>: Hi, Camilo. How was your class? </br>\n<strong>Camilo</strong>: It was interesting. We were at Professor Michael's programming class; we read a book about software programming, more specifically, about source codes. </br>\n<strong>Pablo</strong>: I remember something about that. The computer of the enterprise where I work uses that source. </br>\n<strong>Camilo</strong>: As a matter of fact, all computers use it. </br>\n<strong>Pablo</strong>: Ok, can you explain that to me? </br>", "image": "enpe7n2le01ob05re2img01.jpg", "id": 0}, {"time": "26000", "text": "<strong>Camilo</strong>: A source code is a collection of computer instructions in an easy computer language, as an ordinary text that facilitates the job of computer programmers. There are some specific features to consider, for example, the assembler. </br>\n<strong>Pablo</strong>: What does the assembler do? </br>\n<strong>Camilo</strong>: The assembler or compiler transforms the source code into binary machine code that the computer can understand. Then the computer stores the machine code and interprets the source code for execution. </br>", "image": "enpe7n2le01ob05re2img02.jpg", "id": 1}, {"time": "59000", "text": "<strong>Pablo</strong>: Why is source code important? </br>\n<strong>Camilo</strong>: Programmers use the source code as an input to the process that produces programs. They can also use it as a method of communicating language algorithms; besides that, computer programmers often find it helpful when they need to review existing source code to learn how to transform programming techniques. </br>\n<strong>Pablo</strong>: So, what other features of source code did you identify? </br>\n<strong>Camilo</strong>: I found that programmers write source codes in different programming languages in order to optimize purposes. What is more, I recognized that the program was part of a source tree, and that the source code stored algorithms on the computer's hard disk as well as in a database. </br>", "image": "enpe7n2le01ob05re2img03.jpg", "id": 2}], "audiosrc": "enpe7n2le01ob05re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "title": "", "id": 4, "type": "audio"}], "id": 0, "type": "scholar"}]}